// assets/catalog/units.ron
// Authoritative Mobile Unit Catalog for Space Scuffle (StarCraft II Patch 5.0.14)
//
// `attack_snapshot_cap_ticks`: the longest an attack snapshot lasts, in whole ticks at 25 per
// second (plan `docs/plans/2026-11-24-attacker-snapshot.md` Amendment 1; owner answer Q0112
// 2(c)). A weapon whose `attack_visibility` is `Snapshot` (the default) leaves the player it
// strikes from out of sight a still image of the attacker. The image ends when that player sees
// its spot or the attacker, and at the latest this many ticks after the strike that made it or
// last refreshed it; a later strike by the same attacker on that player moves the image and
// restarts the cap. 25 is 1 second, the owner's starting value. StarCraft II 5.0.14 names no
// duration (the image lasts until seen); `None`, or leaving the field out, restores that.
// Presentation only: no tick decision reads it, so changing it moves no battle, replay or
// checksum. Validated at load: at least 1 (0 would drop every image before it is shown).
//
// `launch_visibility` (a missile weapon's field, beside `attack_visibility`): what the missile's
// release shows of its attacker to the player whose unit it is aimed at, StarCraft II's
// CEffectLaunchMissile `Visibility` (plan 2026-11-27-launch-and-spell-visibility D-1). Omitted,
// the engine default `Snapshot` (core EffectData:102), which no 5.0.14 weapon launch overrides:
// the image is made when the missile leaves, a flight time before the impact's. Only the
// Mothership Carrier's salvo names it, `Hidden`, because its game counterpart launches no missile
// (bug B-22; plan 2026-11-27-weapon-delivery D-7). `Visible(reveal_ticks: N)` and `Hidden` are
// accepted on a missile weapon only.
//
// `missile_movers` (a missile weapon's field): StarCraft II's CEffectLaunchMissile `Movers`, the
// range bands of speed phases its missile may fly (plan 2026-11-27-weapon-delivery D-2). Each
// mover is `(up_to_range, phases)`: chosen at the release when the edge-to-edge distance is at
// most `up_to_range` (`IfRangeLTE`; `None` on the last mover, which admits any distance); each
// phase `(speed, acceleration, max_speed, ends)` in world units per tick and per tick squared (a
// Normal speed v is 0.056 v per tick, a Normal acceleration a is 0.003136 a), `speed` `None`
// carrying the speed in and `ends` where the next phase starts (`None` on the last phase only):
// `Flown(x)` once the path flown since the release reaches x (a positive `Outro`, its midpoint),
// `Remaining(x)` once at most x is left to the impact (a negative `Outro`, its magnitude; plan
// 2026-11-28-missile-movers-b52 D-2). With movers, `projectile_speed` is the missile's top speed.
// Omitted: a constant `projectile_speed`.
//
// `capabilities.strike_magazine` (plan 2026-11-28-broodlings D-3): StarCraft II's CAbilArmMagazine
// whose members are never units of their own (the Brood Lord's escorts), `(capacity, start,
// build_ticks, arming_ticks)`: at most `capacity` charges armed, arming and building together,
// `start` armed when the unit is created, one built at a time in `build_ticks` and armed
// `arming_ticks` after its build. A release of the unit's weapon carries one armed charge per
// strike, up to `attacks_count`; with none armed the weapon starts no swing. Omitted: none.
//
// `impact_spawn` (a missile weapon's field; plan 2026-11-28-broodlings D-4, D-5): StarCraft II's
// `FinishEffect` CEffectCreateUnit, `(unit, per_strike, search_range, timed_life, order)`: where
// the missile's flight finishes, hit or miss (at the target, or the last point if it was lost; a
// missile that fizzles creates nothing), `per_strike` units of the slug `unit` per strike it
// carried, placed within `search_range` world units, each with `timed_life: Some((ticks,
// random_extra_ticks))` (dies after `ticks` plus 0 to `random_extra_ticks` at random, with no
// damage source) or `None`, and the first order `AttackTargetOrPoint` (attack the target if it
// can, else attack-move to the finish). The unit exists only by spawning: no structure trains
// it, it costs no supply and spawns nothing in turn. Omitted: none.
(
    attack_snapshot_cap_ticks: Some(25),
    units: [
